course: dictionary
lesson: 4258
title: Feeling grateful
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Grateful is an adjective, so it describes a feeling. It means you feel thankful to someone because they helped you or gave you something, and you want to show it. «Grateful people tend to be happier and kinder.» Noticing good things and saying thank you is part of being grateful.
explain: Grateful often comes with for or to. You are grateful for something, like a gift, and grateful to someone, like a teacher who helped you. «Afterwards Toad sends the gaoler's daughter a gold chain and a modest, grateful letter.» The letter shows Toad's thanks, so the word grateful tells you how he felt.
explain: Feelings can be mixed. «You can feel disappointed and grateful at the same time.» Feeling both does not make you a bad person. Grateful can also be a polite way to ask for something: «I'd be grateful if you could pass the salt.»
fact: Grateful means feeling thankful for help or a gift, and wanting to show it.
fact: Use grateful for a thing: grateful for your help. Use grateful to a person: grateful to someone.
fact: Saying thank you, or writing a card, is a way of showing you are grateful.
fact: Many schools use gratitude journals, where you write «three things I am grateful for».
fact: «I'd be grateful if…» is a polite way to ask someone to do something.
exercise: «Marco said, "Come with us, my uncle's has an extra ticket." Darnell felt sad, then grateful.» What does grateful mean here? | *Thankful because a friend included him | Tired after a long walk | Bored of the trip | Angry and loud
exercise: Which word fits the gap? «I am ___ to my teacher for helping me with my reading.» | famished | glum | *grateful | curt
exercise: «I'd be grateful if you could pass the salt.» What is this sentence doing? | Saying goodbye | Shouting an order | Telling a joke | *Asking politely
test: Which word means thankful for help or a gift? | Curt | Glum | *Grateful | Barely
test: Grateful ___ someone. Which small word fits the gap? | blue | on | *to | with
exam: «You can feel disappointed and grateful at the same time.» What does this tell you? | *Feelings can be mixed, and feeling both does not make you a bad person | You must never feel disappointed | Only adults can feel grateful | Disappointed and grateful mean exactly the same
